Question:
\text{Water is flowing into an empty right circular cone at a constant rate of }  8\,\text{cm}^3  \text{ per minute. The depth of the liquid in the cone at time, }  t,  \text{ in minutes, is }  x\,\text{cm}. 
\text{The angle, }  \alpha,  \text{ between the perpendicular height, }  h,  \text{ of the cone and the slant height is}
 \tan^{(-$2)} \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}  \text{ and the volume of the cone can be calculated as }  V = \frac{1}{3} \pi r^2 h. 
\text{(i) Show that the volume, }  V\,\text{cm}^3,  \text{ of water in the cone when the depth is }  x\,\text{cm}  \text{ can be}
\text{expressed as }  V = \frac{1}{9} \pi x^3.
